    "video_jMcjHJ": {
      "type": "video",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_FekL7B": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The Story of Ameda – The Breast Pump Originator",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_z9mzwi": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>In 1942, Ameda's founder, Swedish engineer Einar Egnell, was challenged by a leading gynecologist to create a better breast pump. After extensive research and trials, Egnell developed the first hospital-grade pump that mimicked an infant's natural suckling rhythm, making it more comfortable for moms while ensuring effective milk expression.</p><p>Egnell's commitment to improving breastfeeding technology led to the creation of Ameda, and he established the vacuum and cycling standards that are still the industry benchmark today. For over 80 years, we have continued his mission to innovate and deliver the highest quality breast pump technology.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
